# spec_id: eravos.pitch-notes · version 1.0.0 · status built (3.254, 2026-11-27) · template eravos.tool/1
# his words (2026-11-27): "Also tools to connect to tools." · "Voice tools. Like recording. Making sound like the tools? …"
identity:
  id: eravos.pitch-notes ; label: Pitch → Notes ; domain: music ; family: modulation (connect) ; accent: "#b48cff"
  lineage: pitch-to-MIDI converters; a connector, and the Voice Lab's first step from a voice to the tools (specs/eravos.voice-lab.spec)
assembles (components, tools/music/components/<id>/ — never re-implemented here):
  pitch-tracker
signal_dag:
  in → pitch-tracker
  pitch-tracker → out
engine: one AudioWorklet (the component's kernel text): in (a tap) → PitchTracker (Lowest, Highest, Hears from) → the nearest note; when it
  holds for Settle (and is not the note already playing) a message with the note, its cents off and the time of its first reading →
  snapped into the key (In key), Octave, Length fitted to the beat, Velocity from the level → a note on every tool wired to Notes, booked at
  that time. Silence ends the note heard. Pitch out: the line, 0…1 across MIDI 0–127, continuously.
ports: in (audio, tap, primary) · out: Notes (note:trigger) · Pitch (mod)
packs: factory — Voice Plays Keys · Voice Plays Bass · Lead Doubles · Slow Chords Root · Exact (no key) · Hum To Melody
open: a note held for as long as it is sung (ERAVOS notes carry their length from the start); polyphony (the tracker hears one line)
acceptance (pitch-notes.test.js, P246): a line A3 · C4 · E4 · silence · A4 → those 4 notes, each booked within 80 ms of its start (one 43 ms frame of the new note must be heard to name it); In key snaps
  a C#4 into A minor; Octave −1 moves them down; a sung vowel (a pulse train through formants) reads its note; it only listens

